<h1>Help</h1>
<p>Each row in the list is a <strong>key</strong> of OpenCutList's interface: on the left is 
the reference text (either the French original or the English translation, depending on your 
selection above the column), and on the right is your translation. Write your translation, 
then click Save to save it without leaving the page.
</p>

<h2>Statuses</h2>
<dl>
  <dt class="flex h-6 items-center gap-2 self-start"><%= status_dot "outdated" %> <strong>To review</strong></dt><dd>The French text has changed since your translation. Check it, fix it if needed, then save, even unchanged, to validate it again. Or an open issue questions it, whatever its kind: fix it if needed, then mark the issue resolved. It can't be approved before.</dd>
  <dt class="flex h-6 items-center gap-2 self-start"><%= status_dot "not_translated" %> <strong>Not translated</strong></dt><dd>Nothing written in your language yet.</dd>
  <dt class="flex h-6 items-center gap-2 self-start"><%= status_dot "not_approved" %> <strong>Not approved</strong></dt><dd>Translated, but not approved yet.</dd>
  <dt class="flex h-6 items-center gap-2 self-start"><%= status_dot "approved" %> <strong>Approved</strong></dt><dd>Approved by a reviewer of the language.</dd>
</dl>
<p>Reviewers have an <strong>Approve</strong> button next to <strong>Save</strong>. An approved text should only be modified with care!</p>

<h2>The Editor</h2>
<ul>
  <li>
    Some parts of the French text must be used as-is in the translation: variables <code>{{ count }}</code>, references
    to other keys <code>$t(tab.cutlist.title)</code>, HTML tags <code>&lt;strong&gt;</code> and entities
    <code>&amp;nbsp;</code>. They are <strong>locked</strong>: you can move them within the sentence, not change them. When
    one is missing, a chip under the editor puts it back; an unknown one shows in red.
  </li>
  <li><kbd>⌘</kbd>-click (<kbd>Ctrl</kbd>-click) on a <code>$t(…)</code> reference opens the key it points to in a new tab.</li>
  <li>
    Keep the Markdown: <code>**bold**</code>, <code>*italic*</code>, links <code>[text](url)</code>. Translate the link's
    text, keep its url (or adapt it if there is a language version that matches your language).
  </li>
  <li>
    <strong>Proposals</strong> under the editor (<%= robot_icon("text-violet-500") %> machine translation, "Same text elsewhere") can be filled with one click.
    Read it again before saving.
  </li>
  <li>
    <strong>Warnings</strong> ⚠ (final dot, spaces, line count…) do not prevent saving: they indicate what requires attention.
  </li>
  <li>Greyed keys are <strong>copied</strong> as-is into every language: nothing to translate.</li>
  <li>
    Above the list, <kbd>¶</kbd> shows spaces and line breaks, the key button always shows the keys' names (otherwise on
    hover only).
  </li>
  <li>If you have made changes to a translation that have not yet been saved, the background will be blue. 
  The page will warn you before you leave if you have any unsaved changes.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Shortcuts</h2>
<dl>
  <dt><kbd>⌘/Ctrl</kbd> + <kbd>Enter</kbd></dt><dd>Save</dd>
  <dt><kbd>⌘/Ctrl</kbd> + <kbd>Shift</kbd> + <kbd>Enter</kbd></dt><dd>Save and approve (reviewers)</dd>
  <dt><kbd>⌘/Ctrl</kbd> + <kbd>F</kbd></dt><dd>Go to the search (a 2nd time: the browser's)</dd>
  <dt><kbd>Esc</kbd></dt><dd>Leave the search field</dd>
  <dt><kbd>Esc</kbd> <kbd>Esc</kbd></dt><dd>Clear the search, filters and sort</dd>
</dl>

<h2>Search and Filters</h2>
<p>
  The search looks through the texts, ignoring case and accents. The <strong>Filters</strong> menu narrows the list by status, to open questions,
  warnings or recently changed keys; the <strong>Sort</strong> menu orders the list by modification date. In the search field,
  before pressing <kbd>Enter</kbd>:
</p>
<dl>
  <dt><code>#120</code>, <code>#120-180</code></dt><dd>by row number</dd>
  <dt><code>key:…</code></dt><dd>by key name</dd>
  <dt><code>branch:…</code></dt><dd>by branch (<code>tab.cutlist</code>)</dd>
  <dt><code>user:…</code></dt><dd>by author (name or its start)</dd>
  <dt><code>"Word "</code></dt><dd>exact text between quotes: spaces, case and accents included</dd>
</dl>

<h2>Asking a Question</h2>
<p>
  Unsure what a text means? The <strong>comments</strong> button under each translation lets you ask a question about
  that key: the admins and your language's reviewers are notified, and the answer shows in the same place. For anything else
  (access, a new language, a problem with the tool…), write to us with the form.
</p>
